  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Crew creation",
    "section": "19.15",
    "heading": "Cohort harm & Healing",
    "lineStart": 1479,
    "lineEnd": 1490
  },
  "section": "19.15",
  "rulesText": "Cohorts suffer harm similarly to PCs. A cohort can suffer four levels of harm:\n\n* **Weakened.** The cohort has reduced effect.\n* **Impaired.** The cohort operates with reduced quality (-1d).\n* **Broken.** The cohort can't do anything until they recover.\n* **Dead.** The cohort is destroyed.\n\nAll of your cohorts heal during downtime. If circumstances are amenable for recovery, each cohort removes one level of harm (or two levels of harm instead, if a PC spends a downtime activity helping them recuperate).\n\nIf a cohort is destroyed, it may be replaced. Spend **coin** equal to your Tier +2 to restore it, plus two downtime activities to recruit new gang members, or hire a new expert."
}
